# CLAUDE.md

Per-repo orientation for `${git_provider.org}/${project_name}` — Docusaurus
aggregator site that pulls `docs/` from every homelab repo at build time.

## Homelab universals

- **Toolchain pinned via `mise.toml`**; task runner `just`.
- **`.env` is a [1Password Developer Environment](https://developer.1password.com/docs/environments/local-env-file)** file. `op run --env-file=.env -- <cmd>`. Never `source .env`.
- **`docz create <type> "Title"`** for new docs that live HERE.
- **`grep` is `rg`** — drop `-E`.

## Repo layout

```
docusaurus.config.js   # site config + remote-content plugin sources
sidebars.js            # left-nav structure
docs/                  # native pages (cross-cutting topics that don't fit elsewhere)
  runbooks/
  architecture/
  ...
src/                   # custom Docusaurus components / pages (if any)
static/                # static assets
package.json
```

## Conventions

- **Remote-content plugin = aggregation, NOT mirror**. Each repo's
  `docs/` is fetched at build time from its source location. No
  committed mirror, no sync workflow, no per-repo PR-to-sync. Source of
  truth stays in each originating repo.
- **Native pages** in `docs/` are for content that genuinely belongs at
  the homelab level: runbooks that span repos, network topology
  overviews, multi-repo architecture diagrams. Per-repo content lives
  in the per-repo `docs/`.
- **Build deploys to `https://docs.fartlab.dev`** (or chosen domain) via
  `.forgejo/workflows/build-deploy.yml`. Static output published to
  Garage S3 / a CDN / GitHub Pages — TBD.

## Sources (TODO: wire up)

The remote-content plugin needs auth for private Forgejo repos. Options:

1. **Forgejo PAT** with `read:repository` scope on the homelab org.
   Stored in 1P, exposed via `op run` at build time. Simplest.
2. **Forgejo Actions OIDC** federated to a service-account token —
   more secure but more setup.

Source list (initial):

- `git.fartlab.dev/homelab/k8s/docs/` → `/k8s/`
